WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.106
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.406 --> 00:00:08.503
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.803 --> 00:00:14.299
Unit seventeen: Law and Order. In this unit, you will talk about justice and the legal system.

4
00:00:15.283 --> 00:00:16.250
justice.

5
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.994
justice means fair treatment according to the law.

6
00:00:20.294 --> 00:00:22.317
The victims' families want justice.

7
00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:25.692
Your turn. Say: justice.

8
00:00:28.392 --> 00:00:29.440
justice.

9
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.172
trial.

10
00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:35.114
trial means a formal examination of a case in a court.

11
00:00:35.414 --> 00:00:37.274
The trial lasted three weeks.

12
00:00:37.974 --> 00:00:39.872
Your turn. Say: trial.

13
00:00:42.572 --> 00:00:43.306
trial.

14
00:00:44.317 --> 00:00:45.271
sentence.

15
00:00:45.971 --> 00:00:48.598
sentence means the punishment given by a judge.

16
00:00:48.898 --> 00:00:51.350
He received a sentence of five years in prison.

17
00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.331
Your turn. Say: sentence.

18
00:00:57.031 --> 00:00:57.962
sentence.

19
00:00:58.950 --> 00:00:59.684
jury.

20
00:01:00.384 --> 00:01:03.881
jury means a group of citizens who decide if someone is guilty.

21
00:01:04.181 --> 00:01:05.983
The jury found him not guilty.

22
00:01:06.683 --> 00:01:08.593
Your turn. Say: jury.

23
00:01:11.293 --> 00:01:12.085
jury.

24
00:01:13.083 --> 00:01:14.259
legal system.

25
00:01:14.959 --> 00:01:17.887
legal system means the laws and courts of a country.

26
00:01:18.187 --> 00:01:21.115
Every legal system should be fair and independent.

27
00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:24.665
Your turn. Say: legal system.

28
00:01:27.365 --> 00:01:28.587
legal system.

29
00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:30.863
human rights law.

30
00:01:31.563 --> 00:01:35.269
human rights law means laws that protect people's basic freedoms.

31
00:01:35.569 --> 00:01:38.091
Human rights law protects freedom of speech.

32
00:01:38.791 --> 00:01:41.397
Your turn. Say: human rights law.

33
00:01:44.097 --> 00:01:45.354
human rights law.

34
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.084
appeal.

35
00:01:47.784 --> 00:01:50.678
appeal means asking a higher court to change a decision.

36
00:01:50.978 --> 00:01:53.116
His lawyer will appeal against the decision.

37
00:01:53.816 --> 00:01:56.051
Your turn. Say: appeal.

38
00:01:58.751 --> 00:01:59.624
appeal.

39
00:02:00.617 --> 00:02:01.618
prosecutor.

40
00:02:02.318 --> 00:02:05.409
prosecutor means a lawyer who argues that someone is guilty.

41
00:02:05.709 --> 00:02:07.813
The prosecutor presented new evidence.

42
00:02:08.513 --> 00:02:10.712
Your turn. Say: prosecutor.

43
00:02:13.412 --> 00:02:14.483
prosecutor.

44
00:02:15.483 --> 00:02:17.506
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:17.806 --> 00:02:20.549
My uncle got his car stolen last month.

46
00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:25.002
I'm sorry to hear that. Did the police catch the thief?

47
00:02:26.317 --> 00:02:29.988
Yes, and he's getting his case heard in court next week.

48
00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:33.062
Will there be a trial with a jury?

49
00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:39.255
Cambodia's legal system doesn't use juries. A judge decides the sentence.

50
00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:43.411
I see. And if he disagrees, he can appeal.

51
00:02:44.717 --> 00:02:47.320
Grammar focus: Passive with get and have.

52
00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:52.882
Get plus past participle is an informal passive, often for unexpected events.

53
00:02:53.182 --> 00:02:57.480
Have plus something plus past participle can describe something bad that happened to you.

54
00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:02.276
For example: She had her bag stolen at the market, and the thief got caught on camera.

55
00:03:02.576 --> 00:03:07.234
Have something done can describe a service (I had my hair cut) or an unpleasant event (I had my phone stolen).

56
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.508
Now read and listen. How Courts Work.

57
00:03:10.808 --> 00:03:14.363
Different countries organise their legal systems in different ways.

58
00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:20.343
In some countries, a jury of ordinary citizens decides whether a person is guilty.

59
00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:26.030
In others, like Cambodia, professional judges hear the case and decide the sentence.

60
00:03:27.317 --> 00:03:31.394
Both the prosecutor and the defence lawyer present evidence during the trial.

61
00:03:32.683 --> 00:03:36.529
If either side believes the decision is unfair, they can make an appeal.

62
00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:40.306
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:40.606 --> 00:03:44.429
A group of citizens who decide if someone is guilty is a blank.

64
00:03:44.729 --> 00:03:47.964
A, jury. B, trial. C, prosecutor.

65
00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:53.578
The answer is A: jury.

66
00:03:55.083 --> 00:03:57.083
He got blank for driving too fast.

67
00:03:57.383 --> 00:04:00.258
A, stop. B, stopped. C, stopping.

68
00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.052
The answer is B: stopped.

69
00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:09.550
I had my wallet blank on the bus.

70
00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:13.108
A, steal. B, stolen. C, stealing.

71
00:04:17.117 --> 00:04:18.617
The answer is B: stolen.

72
00:04:20.117 --> 00:04:23.115
Asking a higher court to change a decision is an blank.

73
00:04:23.415 --> 00:04:26.569
A, appeal. B, sentence. C, justice.

74
00:04:30.583 --> 00:04:32.211
The answer is A: appeal.

75
00:04:33.717 --> 00:04:37.017
According to the text, who decides the sentence in Cambodia?

76
00:04:37.317 --> 00:04:41.167
A, a jury. B, professional judges. C, the police.

77
00:04:45.183 --> 00:04:47.845
The answer is B: professional judges.

78
00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:53.651
Now it's your turn to speak. Why is a fair legal system important for a country?

79
00:04:58.951 --> 00:05:05.853
It protects everyone equally. If people get treated unfairly, they lose trust in justice and in the government.

80
00:05:06.153 --> 00:05:07.850
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:12.652
Great work today! You learned eight new words and passive with get and have.

82
00:05:12.952 --> 00:05:15.964
Today's value is honesty. Always tell the truth.

83
00:05:16.264 --> 00:05:18.405
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

84
00:05:18.705 --> 00:05:21.253
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

